From 2c15cfb2004d8e4cc57fe1198e0c0e983436bb72 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 07:32:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): wire flow evidence and daily admission recovery
 [daveey]

Address all five behavioral findings and three nits from independent review
of PR #3742 at 7c4f31e53ca2:
- Read awaiting from the current scheduled event; supersede review_requested
  on changes_requested; preserve creator-task provenance.
- Read PR state/review/required checks within a five-second per-report budget,
  deduplicated by URL; fence OPEN observations on unchanged head and decision.
  Missing checks are not green. Explicit matching live-readback observations
  expose test; merge time alone never proves installation.
- Reconsider daily-limit-only parks in home-owned readiness maintenance,
  respecting foreign copies, containment, ordinary lane gates and available
  capacity. Enforce both caps in transactional planner admissions and preserve
  admitted-parent review exemptions.
- Count actual admissions (including unbudgeted admits), not re-lanes or
  explicitly parked creation. Retain compatibility with legacy creation events.
- Remove dead reason branches; document reported-cost-only spend coverage.

Five whys: helper-only tests encoded normalized dictionaries rather than the
real event and readiness paths; no producer populated tasks.awaiting or the
PR flags those tests supplied. Persisted-event tests and an executed gh fixture
now exercise those seams, and reset tests recheck an already-held card.

Proof:
- RED: 8 daily-cap regression failures and 10 persisted-evidence failures.
- GREEN: canonical core-wt runner: 12 files, 1724 passed, 0 failed.
  Includes 33 original flow and 39 new cap/evidence/PR-reader tests.
- Mutation baseline 39 passed; 17/17 mutants killed. The initial gate-reason
  survivor led to a real capped/manual-admission case, then killed on rerun.
- scripts/check --base origin/main: all 21 checks passed.
- Live hub config readback: all five lanes leave both new caps unset; zero
  recorded daily-limit parks. This PR does not enable limits in production.

Hotspot: kanban_db.py readiness delegates to the topical daily-limit module.
The unchanged _latest_event query is moved behind its existing wrapper to keep
the facade under its existing line cap.

